# round-31 R2 guard: the removed `.str()` (and any unknown primitive method)
# must ALSO reject inside an f-string interpolation `f"{...}"`. The f-string
# path used to `errors.truncate` ALL interpolation errors — silently swallowing
# genuine method-existence errors (and `.str()` was used MOST inside f-strings).
# The reject (#1) would be defeated exactly here without the split_off + retain
# filter (typecheck.rs, #2). If this fixture ever passes `gg check`, the
# f-string error-swallow regressed.
void main():
    String s = "hi"
    print(f"{s.str()}")
